#: ../../../lib/_autosummary/helpers/xonsh.tools.rst:2
msgid "xonsh.tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:1
msgid "Shared utility functions and helpers for the xonsh shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:3
msgid ""
"This module is the grab-bag of small, broadly-useful helpers used across the "
"xonsh codebase — anything that doesn't naturally fit into one of the more "
"focused subsystems (parser, execer, environ, procs, completers, prompt, "
"history) ends up here. Downstream code — including xontribs — can import "
"from :mod:`xonsh.tools` as a stable public API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:9
msgid "The module groups its helpers roughly by topic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:11
msgid ""
"**Exceptions and error handling** — :class:`XonshError`, :class:"
"`XonshCalledProcessError`, :func:`print_exception`, :func:"
"`format_std_prepost`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:14
msgid ""
"**Type conversion and validation** — the ``is_*`` / ``to_*`` / "
"``*_or_default`` family used by :class:`~xonsh.environ.Env` to validate and "
"normalise environment variables (bools, ints, paths, lists, dicts, history "
"units, log levels, color schemes, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:18
msgid ""
"**Path and file utilities** — :func:`expand_path`, :func:"
"`expanduser_abs_path`, :func:`is_writable_file`, :func:`executables_in`, :"
"func:`iglobpath`, cross-platform path normalisation helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:22
msgid ""
"**String, token and AST helpers** — quoting/escaping, :func:"
"`subexpr_from_unbalanced`, :func:`find_next_break`, regex constants for "
"string prefixes and history tuples, the :class:`FlexibleFormatter` for "
"prompt/format-string rendering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:26
msgid ""
"**Subprocess and signal helpers** — :func:`on_main_thread`, :func:"
"`suggest_commands`, signal-safe context managers, PTY helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:28
msgid ""
"**Terminal and color handling** — ANSI/ANSI256/RGB color parsing, "
"``PTK_NEW_OLD_COLOR_MAP``, ``WIN10_COLOR_MAP`` and related lookup tables, :"
"func:`print_color` / :func:`format_color`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:31
msgid ""
"**Collections and functional helpers** — :class:`LazyObject`, :class:"
"`LazyDict`, :class:`DefaultNotGivenType`, ``always_true``, ``always_false``, "
"``all_permutations``, small functional shims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:34
msgid ""
"**Platform and environment probes** — Windows/POSIX conditionals, locale "
"detection, terminal-size queries, shell-level (``SHLVL``) adjustment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/tools.py:docstring of xonsh.tools:38
msgid ""
"A handful of the oldest helpers (``decode``, ``encode``, ``cast_unicode``, "
"``safe_hasattr``, ``indent``) were originally forked from the IPython "
"project and retain their upstream copyrights:"
msgstr ""

